<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
App Group + iCloud/CloudKit entitlements for YTMusicApp.

APP GROUP: Grants this app access to the group.com.landonkea.ytmusic shared
container, which is how AudioPlayer hands "now playing" state to the
YTMusicWidget extension (see Sources/YTMusicShared/NowPlayingSnapshot.swift
for the full explanation). YTMusicWidget.entitlements declares the SAME
group string — both targets must list an identical App Group for the shared
container to resolve to the same place for each process.

ICLOUD/CLOUDKIT: Grants access to the iCloud.com.landonkea.ytmusic private
CloudKit container, used by CloudKitSyncManager (see
Sources/YTMusicApp/Services/CloudKitSyncManager.swift) to sync the user's
playlists and liked songs — and ONLY those two things, not listening
stats — across their devices. The container identifier follows this app's
existing App-Group naming convention (group.com.landonkea.ytmusic ->
iCloud.com.landonkea.ytmusic).

NOTE ON LOCAL/CI BUILDS WITHOUT A SIGNING TEAM: Both App Groups and iCloud
containers are normally provisioned through a paid Apple Developer account.
In this repo (no committed signing team, "sign to run locally" style local
builds), UserDefaults(suiteName:) against the App Group may resolve to nil,
and CKContainer operations against the iCloud container will fail (no
account / no real container) rather than sync anything. Both failure paths
are handled gracefully in code: NowPlayingSnapshotStore treats a nil App
Group container as "shared state unavailable" and no-ops; CloudKitSyncManager
catches the container/zone-creation error and logs+skips the sync pass
rather than crashing (see performSync() in CloudKitSyncManager.swift). The
app's own local playlists/liked songs/playback are unaffected either way —
only cross-device sync and the widget's shared state require a real
provisioning profile with these capabilities configured.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.landonkea.ytmusic</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.com.landonkea.ytmusic</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudKit</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
